  {
   "id": "FxIh-uwOAwAJ",
   "from": "Daniel Morillo Cuadrado",
   "author": "38226bd700051927",
   "date": "2023-12-17T12:23:31Z",
   "subject": "Re: Error When Using Sampling.Weights with FIML.x",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I&#39;d say you may have either of the following two issues (or some combination of both):</div><div></div><div><ul><li>You have a large n, so when weights are normalised (i.e. so that they sum up to 1), they all get so small they become &quot;computational zeros&quot;.</li><li>Your valid cases (the ones actually being used to fit the model) all have a zero weight value.<br></li></ul></div><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span>Not really sure how to solve it; without a reprex one can experiment with it&#39;s difficult to find a solution, but you can try filtering out the cases with a zero-weight and see what happens. It may not be the optimal solution but it can point you in the right direction.</span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span><br></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span>Hope it helps,</span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span>Daniel<br></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span>--</span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Daniel Morillo, Ph.D.</span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"></span></font></div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/DaniMori\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/DaniMori&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792415189133000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0g0RcVB6ulz8dl-EZlyYQI\">GitHub</a> | <a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3021-3878\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3021-3878&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792415189133000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1hTKlqpxGLyu8Ke-TeAMsM\">\r\nORCID</a></span></font></div></div></div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
